meta {
  name: refresh with HAR
  type: http
  seq: 7
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/internal/rcs/pair/refresh
  body: none
  auth: none
}

docs {
  Re-authenticates a phone that is **already paired**, using fresh cookies. No
  emoji to tap, no re-pairing, and the phone does not have to do anything.

  This is the recurring chore for phones paired by HAR. The symptom that you
  need it: `health` shows `connected: false` with a `lastError` mentioning HTTP
  401, and the health monitor logs that the Google session has expired and
  needs a refresh.

  Same upload shape as `pair with HAR` — the .har as the raw body:

  ```
  curl -X POST http://localhost:8080/internal/rcs/pair/refresh \
       --data-binary "@fresh.har"
  ```

  The cookies must belong to the **same Google account** the phone is paired to.
  A mismatch is rejected rather than silently re-pairing to the wrong account.

  On success the stored session is updated and the phone reconnects on its own.
  Nothing needs restarting.

  **Phones paired by QR never need this.** If you find yourself running it
  daily, it is worth re-checking whether that handset offers a QR scanner, since
  that removes the chore entirely.

  Errors:
  - 400 — no session stored yet, so pair first rather than refresh
  - 400 — bad or expired cookies, or cookies for a different Google account
}
